# UI Design System — Luxury, Premium, Powerful

High-end gym / fitness-studio aesthetic. Modern, professional, dark theme with gold accents.

## Palette — define once in the Tailwind theme, never use raw hex in components

| Token      | Hex       | Use for |
|------------|-----------|---------|
| background | `#0B0B0B` | main background, sidebar, dashboard background, dark sections |
| primary    | `#F5B800` | primary buttons, active states, highlights, icons, progress indicators, key stats, accent borders |
| secondary  | `#FFFFFF` | headings, important content, primary readable text, cards where appropriate |
| text       | `#A1A1A1` | secondary text, descriptions, labels, metadata |

Do not introduce random colors. Semantic states (success / warning / error) are defined centrally in the
Tailwind theme/constants and reused — never inline hex values.

## Design rules

Use: clean spacing, strong typography, rounded-but-professional cards, subtle borders, clear hierarchy,
consistent shadows, consistent spacing, responsive layouts.

The UI must NOT look cluttered, over-designed, cartoonish, cheap, generic or inconsistent.
Avoid excessive gradients, excessive animations and decorative elements with no purpose.

## Tailwind

- Use Tailwind utilities consistently; no ad-hoc inline styles unless genuinely necessary.
- A repeated style pattern becomes a reusable component (or a centralized class), not copy-pasted utility strings.
- Keep padding, margin, font sizes, border radius, shadows, colors and breakpoints consistent across the app.

## Responsive

Support desktop, laptop, tablet and mobile. The admin dashboard must work on small screens.
Tables need proper responsive behavior; never allow unnecessary horizontal overflow.
